@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;capacity] native-flow-read-only-bounded
The helper MUST issue only a single exact conntrack GET in its inherited
namespace, with canonical tuple arguments and a two-second process deadline.
It MUST NOT dump, create, update or delete conntrack entries or change
namespace. No setuid or capabilities; stdout carries only the 128-bit label.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] flow-label-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover canonical IPv4/port parsing, label bit endianness
against a big-endian u128 oracle, the `Labels::to_hex` round-trip through an
independent decoder and the match/reject matrix with an independent spec. The
kernel GET sits behind a typed FFI shim; stale-flow acceptance evidence stays
with the networking machine tests.
